  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5g}\u00f7\\frac{3}{10{g}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5g}\u00f7\\frac{3}{10{g}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{5g}\\cdot \\frac{10{g}^{2}}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\cancel{5}\\cdot \\cancel{g}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{5}\\cdot 2\\cdot {g}^{\\cancel{2}}}{3} & = \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{2g}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{8g}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
